From: V-PACE <yocto@vpace>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_camera: add time_per_frame parameter (VIDIOC_S_PARM)

Stock v4l2_camera has no way to set the capture frame rate. It requests a format
and starts streaming, leaving the device at whatever interval the format defaults
to -- 30 fps for our Logitech Brio 100. There is no version to upgrade to: 0.6.2
(humble), 0.7.1 (jazzy), 0.8.0 (rolling) and upstream master all lack the
parameter, and none of them calls VIDIOC_S_PARM anywhere.

The consequence is worse than a missing feature, because a `time_per_frame` key
in a params YAML looks like it works. rclcpp keeps unknown keys as parameter
overrides and discards them without a warning, so our camera_params.yaml asked
for 2 fps for months while the camera ran at 30 fps, doing 15x the intended
TensorRT inference and pushing 18.4 MB/s of throwaway YUYV over a USB 2.0 bus
shared with the WiFi dongle.

Setting the rate from outside the node is not a workaround. VIDIOC_S_FMT resets
the frame interval to the format default, so an external S_PARM is undone the
moment the node applies its format. Measured on target: set 1/5, start the node
with a differing image_size, and G_PARM reads back 1/30 with the topic at 28 Hz.
It only appears to survive when the requested format happens to equal the current
one, because requestImageSize() returns early in that case and skips S_FMT --
an accident that breaks on any fresh boot, replug or resolution change.

The parameter is modelled on the one in tier4's fork
(https://github.com/tier4/ros2_v4l2_camera), with three deliberate differences:

  - It is declared unconditionally, even on devices that report no
    V4L2_CAP_TIMEPERFRAME. A declared parameter that logs a warning is far easier
    to debug than an undeclared one that vanishes silently -- which is the exact
    failure this patch exists to remove.

  - applyParameters() applies it *after* the pixel format and image size, and
    handleParameter() re-applies it after any runtime change to either, because
    of the S_FMT reset described above.

  - V4L2 lets a driver substitute the nearest interval it supports, and S_PARM
    still returns success when it does. We compare the granted value against the
    requested one and warn on a mismatch, so a rate the hardware refused cannot
    be mistaken for one it accepted. Our camera's slowest advertised interval is
    1/5, so a request for [1, 2] lands here.

Verified against v4l2_camera 0.6.2 on a Jetson Orin (L4T r36.5, ROS 2 humble).

diff --git a/include/v4l2_camera/parameters.hpp b/include/v4l2_camera/parameters.hpp
index 71b8f7e..3e97360 100644
--- a/include/v4l2_camera/parameters.hpp
+++ b/include/v4l2_camera/parameters.hpp
@@ -76,6 +76,10 @@ public:
 
   std::string getPixelFormat() const {return getValue<std::string>("pixel_format");}
   std::vector<int64_t> getImageSize() const {return getValue<std::vector<int64_t>>("image_size");}
+  std::vector<int64_t> getTimePerFrame() const
+  {
+    return getValue<std::vector<int64_t>>("time_per_frame");
+  }
 
   std::vector<rclcpp::Parameter> getControlParameters() const
   {
diff --git a/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera.hpp b/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera.hpp
index 1d74d58..6c91e52 100644
--- a/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera.hpp
+++ b/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera.hpp
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@ private:
 
   bool requestPixelFormat(std::string const & fourcc);
   bool requestImageSize(std::vector<int64_t> const & size);
+  bool requestTimePerFrame(std::vector<int64_t> const & timePerFrame);
 
   sensor_msgs::msg::Image::UniquePtr convert(sensor_msgs::msg::Image const & img) const;
 
diff --git a/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera_device.hpp b/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera_device.hpp
index 5eb61df..560e4c1 100644
--- a/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera_device.hpp
+++ b/include/v4l2_camera/v4l2_camera_device.hpp
@@ -67,6 +67,12 @@ public:
   auto const & getCurrentDataFormat() const {return cur_data_format_;}
   bool requestDataFormat(PixelFormat const & format);
 
+  // Frame interval as a (numerator, denominator) fraction of a second,
+  // e.g. {1, 30} is 30 fps. {0, 0} means the device does not support setting it.
+  using TimePerFrame = std::pair<uint32_t, uint32_t>;
+  TimePerFrame getCurrentTimePerFrame() const;
+  bool requestTimePerFrame(TimePerFrame const & timePerFrame);
+
   std::string getCameraName();
 
   sensor_msgs::msg::Image::UniquePtr capture();
diff --git a/src/parameters.cpp b/src/parameters.cpp
index 895a65f..b03c9fd 100644
--- a/src/parameters.cpp
+++ b/src/parameters.cpp
@@ -111,6 +111,22 @@ void Parameters::declareFormatParameters(V4l2CameraDevice const & device)
   declareParameter<std::vector<int64_t>>(
     "image_size", {640, 480}, "Image width & height",
     image_sizes_constraints.str());
+
+  //// time_per_frame
+  // Declared unconditionally, even when the device cannot set it: a declared
+  // parameter that logs a warning is far easier to debug than an undeclared one,
+  // which rclcpp silently discards as an unused parameter override.
+  auto const current_tpf = device.getCurrentTimePerFrame();
+  auto default_tpf = std::vector<int64_t>{
+    static_cast<int64_t>(current_tpf.first == 0 ? 1 : current_tpf.first),
+    static_cast<int64_t>(current_tpf.second == 0 ? 30 : current_tpf.second)};
+
+  declareParameter<std::vector<int64_t>>(
+    "time_per_frame", default_tpf,
+    "Time between two successive frames, as a fraction of a second",
+    "Length 2 array: [numerator, denominator]. [1, 30] is 30 fps, [1, 5] is 5 fps. "
+    "The device may substitute the nearest interval it supports; a warning is logged "
+    "when it does.");
 }
 
 void Parameters::declareControlParameters(V4l2CameraDevice const & device)
diff --git a/src/v4l2_camera.cpp b/src/v4l2_camera.cpp
index 35774d6..b8b18e5 100644
--- a/src/v4l2_camera.cpp
+++ b/src/v4l2_camera.cpp
@@ -153,6 +153,12 @@ void V4L2Camera::applyParameters()
   auto image_size = parameters_.getImageSize();
   requestImageSize(image_size);
 
+  // Time per frame
+  // Must be applied *after* the format requests above: VIDIOC_S_FMT resets the frame
+  // interval back to the format's default, so setting the rate first is silently undone.
+  auto time_per_frame = parameters_.getTimePerFrame();
+  requestTimePerFrame(time_per_frame);
+
   // Control parameters
   auto control_parameters = parameters_.getControlParameters();
   for (auto const & param : control_parameters) {
@@ -220,11 +226,20 @@ bool V4L2Camera::handleParameter(rclcpp::Parameter const & param)
   } else if (param.get_name() == "pixel_format") {
     camera_->stop();
     auto success = requestPixelFormat(param.as_string());
+    // S_FMT resets the frame interval, so restore the configured rate.
+    requestTimePerFrame(parameters_.getTimePerFrame());
     camera_->start();
     return success;
   } else if (param.get_name() == "image_size") {
     camera_->stop();
     auto success = requestImageSize(param.as_integer_array());
+    // S_FMT resets the frame interval, so restore the configured rate.
+    requestTimePerFrame(parameters_.getTimePerFrame());
+    camera_->start();
+    return success;
+  } else if (param.get_name() == "time_per_frame") {
+    camera_->stop();
+    auto success = requestTimePerFrame(param.as_integer_array());
     camera_->start();
     return success;
   } else if (param.get_name() == "camera_info_url") {
@@ -280,6 +295,20 @@ bool V4L2Camera::requestImageSize(std::vector<int64_t> const & size)
   return camera_->requestDataFormat(dataFormat);
 }
 
+bool V4L2Camera::requestTimePerFrame(std::vector<int64_t> const & timePerFrame)
+{
+  if (timePerFrame.size() != 2) {
+    RCLCPP_WARN(
+      get_logger(),
+      "Invalid time per frame; expected dimensions: 2, actual: %lu",
+      timePerFrame.size());
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  return camera_->requestTimePerFrame(
+    {static_cast<uint32_t>(timePerFrame[0]), static_cast<uint32_t>(timePerFrame[1])});
+}
+
 sensor_msgs::msg::Image::UniquePtr V4L2Camera::convert(sensor_msgs::msg::Image const & img) const
 {
   auto tracked_object = std::shared_ptr<const void>{};
diff --git a/src/v4l2_camera_device.cpp b/src/v4l2_camera_device.cpp
index d3605bb..ef44831 100644
--- a/src/v4l2_camera_device.cpp
+++ b/src/v4l2_camera_device.cpp
@@ -311,6 +311,79 @@ bool V4l2CameraDevice::requestDataFormat(const PixelFormat & format)
   return true;
 }
 
+V4l2CameraDevice::TimePerFrame V4l2CameraDevice::getCurrentTimePerFrame() const
+{
+  auto streamParm = v4l2_streamparm{};
+  streamParm.type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE;
+
+  if (-1 == ioctl(fd_, VIDIOC_G_PARM, &streamParm)) {
+    return {0, 0};
+  }
+  if (!(streamParm.parm.capture.capability & V4L2_CAP_TIMEPERFRAME)) {
+    return {0, 0};
+  }
+  return {streamParm.parm.capture.timeperframe.numerator,
+    streamParm.parm.capture.timeperframe.denominator};
+}
+
+bool V4l2CameraDevice::requestTimePerFrame(TimePerFrame const & timePerFrame)
+{
+  if (timePerFrame.first == 0 || timePerFrame.second == 0) {
+    RCLCPP_WARN(
+      rclcpp::get_logger("v4l2_camera"),
+      "Invalid time per frame: %u/%u; both parts must be non-zero",
+      timePerFrame.first, timePerFrame.second);
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  auto streamParm = v4l2_streamparm{};
+  streamParm.type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE;
+
+  if (-1 == ioctl(fd_, VIDIOC_G_PARM, &streamParm)) {
+    RCLCPP_ERROR(
+      rclcpp::get_logger("v4l2_camera"),
+      "Failed reading stream parameters: %s (%s)", strerror(errno),
+      std::to_string(errno).c_str());
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  if (!(streamParm.parm.capture.capability & V4L2_CAP_TIMEPERFRAME)) {
+    RCLCPP_WARN(
+      rclcpp::get_logger("v4l2_camera"),
+      "Device does not support setting the frame interval; ignoring time_per_frame");
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  RCLCPP_INFO(
+    rclcpp::get_logger("v4l2_camera"),
+    "Requesting time per frame: %u/%u", timePerFrame.first, timePerFrame.second);
+
+  streamParm.parm.capture.timeperframe.numerator = timePerFrame.first;
+  streamParm.parm.capture.timeperframe.denominator = timePerFrame.second;
+
+  if (-1 == ioctl(fd_, VIDIOC_S_PARM, &streamParm)) {
+    RCLCPP_ERROR(
+      rclcpp::get_logger("v4l2_camera"),
+      "Failed requesting time per frame: %s (%s)", strerror(errno),
+      std::to_string(errno).c_str());
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  // The driver is allowed to substitute the nearest interval it supports. Say so
+  // loudly rather than reporting success for a rate that is not what was asked for.
+  auto const & granted = streamParm.parm.capture.timeperframe;
+  if (granted.numerator != timePerFrame.first || granted.denominator != timePerFrame.second) {
+    RCLCPP_WARN(
+      rclcpp::get_logger("v4l2_camera"),
+      "Device substituted time per frame %u/%u for the requested %u/%u",
+      granted.numerator, granted.denominator, timePerFrame.first, timePerFrame.second);
+  } else {
+    RCLCPP_INFO(rclcpp::get_logger("v4l2_camera"), "Success");
+  }
+
+  return true;
+}
+
